{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a fascinating film that delves into the origins of facebook, the social media giant that has become an integral part of our lives. directed by david fincher, the movie is a riveting drama that explores the complexities of ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a brilliant and introverted harvard student who creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nas mark navigates the aftermath of facemash, he is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who claim that mark stole their idea for a social networking site called \"harvard connect\". mark agrees to help the winklevosses, but ultimately uses their idea to create his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\".\n\nthe film then follows mark's meteoric rise to success as facebook becomes a global phenomenon, attracting millions of users and generating huge amounts of revenue. however, mark's success comes at a cost, as he becomes increasingly isolated and alienated from his friends and former classmates.\n\none of the most striking aspects of the film is its portrayal of mark zuckerberg, who is depicted as a complex and multifaceted character. jesse eisenberg brings a nuanced and subtle performance to the role, capturing mark's intelligence, ambition, and vulnerability.\n\nthe supporting cast is equally impressive, with andrew garfield delivering a standout performance as eduardo saverin, mark's friend and business partner. the chemistry between eisenberg and garfield is palpable, and their portrayal of the complicated and often fraught relationship between mark and eduardo is compelling.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with a muted color palette and a distinctive visual style that captures the sterile and isolating atmosphere of modern technology. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally effective, adding to the film's tense and unsettling mood.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that raises important questions about the nature of success, friendship, and the impact of technology on our lives. it's a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind one of the most influential companies of our time.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -1.1315475702285767}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0003067976504098624}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.011047860607504845}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " fascinating", "logprob": -2.151057720184326}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.018284693360328674}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0004337085410952568}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.6169659495353699}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -5.829164365422912e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " origins", "logprob": -0.8226742744445801}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.2993727978027891e-05}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.004281165078282356}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.10020658373832703}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011083112098276615}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016780118457973003}, {"token": " media", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " giant", "logprob": -0.03371204808354378}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00032395837479270995}, {"token": " has", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " become", "logprob": -1.7419400215148926}, {"token": " an", "logprob": -2.7656173188006505e-05}, {"token": " integral", "logprob": -1.764281842042692e-05}, {"token": " part", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " of", "logpro